    "priceToIncome": "OECD nominal house price index for Australia divided by ABS average weekly earnings, all employees, persons. The numerator is an index, so the level is index points per dollar of weekly earnings.",
    "qRatio": "Residential land at market plus dwellings at replacement cost, less housing credit outstanding against it, divided by the current replacement cost of the dwellings. The numerator is a mixed balance sheet value. A raw Q of 1 is the theoretical mark where the balance sheet equity equals dwelling replacement cost; it is not an empirical fair value.",
    "detrendedQ": "The raw Q divided by its running geometric mean, using every observation to that date.",
    "ladder": "Each row holds earnings, housing credit and replacement costs at their current levels and moves only the price of the dwelling stock. The 0% row uses the latest reading for each measure."
